      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T05:00:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checked this: the 3 functions that use `max_y \u003d (uint32_t)src_height \u003c\u003c 16` are the box filter functions (`ScalePlaneBox`, `ScalePlaneBox_16`, and `ScaleUVBox`). In those functions, `iy \u003d uy \u003e\u003e 16` is the inclusive start row (computed before `uy +\u003d dy`), and after `uy +\u003d dy` and clamping to `max_y`, `uy \u003e\u003e 16` is the exclusive end row (`boxheight \u003d MIN1((int)(uy \u003e\u003e 16) - iy)`). For the last output row to include the final source row (`src_height - 1`), the exclusive upper bound `uy \u003e\u003e 16` must reach `src_height`, so `max_y` must be `src_height \u003c\u003c 16`. In all other functions (bilinear/simple), `uy` is clamped to `max_y` before extracting `yi \u003d uy \u003e\u003e 16` as a 0-based row index, so the max valid index is `src_height - 1`.",
      "parentUuid": "4122bc4c_2330d67a",
      "revId": "8dabf898eeee2e08d41666ee24533da35f4dcee7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
