        "id": 1115898
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T05:00:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, `FixedDiv(num, div)` is `(num \u003c\u003c 16) / div` (while `FixedDiv1` is `(num - 1) / (div - 1)`), so `FixedDiv(src_height, src_height)` is indeed `1 \u003c\u003c 16`. Looking closer at this `dst_height \u003d\u003d 1 \u0026\u0026 src_height \u003e\u003d 32768` case (here and in `ScaleSlope`), setting `dy \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 16` avoids signed 32-bit overflow in `FixedDiv(32768, 1)`, but it causes `y \u003d CENTERSTART(dy, -32768)` to become `0` (row 0) instead of the center of the image (`(src_height \u003c\u003c 15) - 32768`, row 16383.5). Filed b/573815252 to clean this up and fix the `dst \u003d\u003d 1, src \u003d\u003d 32768` center calculation in a follow-up CL.",
      "parentUuid": "28cf3e76_38346912",
      "revId": "8dabf898eeee2e08d41666ee24533da35f4dcee7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
